			<div class="content" id="post-content-1692461">
									

<p>I can explain it:</p>
<p>The theme of this SCP is that the mundane is horrible. Underneath the most trivial things in our lives &#8212; dishwashers, subways, light fixtures &#8212; there is a pulsing, world-spanning web of living intestines. The existence of that horror is not the responsibility of some external force. It is not an imposition on mundanity.</p>
<p>Rather, the horror comes from precisely the same source as the mundane.</p>
<p>At General Electric, there is apparently someone who understands that dishwashers make an electric wave which attracts the guts &#8212; whatever that means. And he was polite enough to respond. Perhaps he even explained. But we will never know what he said.</p>

